INT. FERRIS WHEEL LOST-AND-FOUND BOOTH - DAY

Cramped. Unclaimed teddy bears. One prosthetic leg.

BARNABY, 50s, attendant, mustache, sits behind a counter. DOT, 70, hands on hips, stands before him.

DOT
I lost a hat.

BARNABY
Describe it.

DOT
Big. Green. A bird on it.

A STRANGER, 40s, slides into frame behind Dot, wearing a green hat with a bird on it. He tips it.

BARNABY
That one?

DOT
That's mine!

The Stranger bolts. Barnaby vaults the counter. Dot swings her purse and misses.

EXT. FERRIS WHEEL BASE - CONTINUOUS

The Stranger climbs into a gondola. Barnaby climbs in after. It lurches skyward.

STRANGER
I'm Wilfred! I found it! It was lost!

BARNABY
It was FOUND by her!

WILFRED
She lost it! I FOUND it! Technically that's the system!

Barnaby considers this. The gondola stops at the top. They both look down at Dot, tiny, waving her purse.

BARNABY
I really hate that you're right.
